    "title": "How to live stream Cruz Azul vs LAFC: Concacaf Champions Cup, TV channel",
    "text": "LAFC travels to Estadio Cuauhtemoc to face Cruz Azul in a quarterfinal Concacaf Champions Cup matchup.MORE: FIFA announces shocking World Cup tailgating decisionWhen: Tuesday, April 14th, 2026Time: 9:00 PM ETTV Channel: Fox Sports 1LAFC hits the road with a 3-0 aggregate lead after handling Cruz Azul at BMO Stadium in the first leg back on April 7th. Son Heung-Min got the scoring started in the 30th minute, with 20-year-old phenom David Martinez finding the back of the net in the 39th minute, leading to a 2-0 halftime lead. Martinez wasn’t finished, as he’d score his second of the game (and fourth of the competition) in the 58th minute, leading to the final score.AdvertisementLive stream Cruz Azul vs LAFC on FuboCruz Azul has played extremely well in domestic competition, currently sitting second in Liga MX with a record of 18-9-4, but that success didn’t translate to the first leg of the Concacaf Champions Cup quarterfinals. One big issue is that they simply didn’t have the ball enough, as they only possessed the ball 34.6% of the time in the first leg. Being under pressure for more than two-thirds of the game led to Cruz Azul clearing the ball a whopping 38 times, compared to just 10 for LAFC.This is a great Concacaf Champions Cup matchup that you will not want to miss; make sure to tune in and catch all the action.Live stream Cruz Azul vs LAFC on Fubo: Start your free trial now!AdvertisementWith Fubo, you can watch live television without cable on your phone, TV, or tablet. Fubo carries a wide array of sports and entertainment channels, including local sports packages and top national channels like ABC, FOX, CBS, ESPN, FS1, MTV, Comedy Central, and much more. The best part is you can try it out today for free.Regional restrictions may apply. If you purchase a product or register for an account through one of the links on our site, we may receive compensation.— Enjoy free coverage of the top news & trending stories on The Big Lead —",
